Returning `new Date().toISOString()` is usually harmless, but health endpoints sometimes get expanded to include version numbers, dependency status, DB connection strings, etc. Establish discipline now: keep `/health` minimal and unauthenticated, put richer diagnostics behind auth at `/health/detailed`.

