Express does not set hardening headers by default. Missing headers like `X-Content-Type-Options`, `Strict-Transport-Security`, `Content-Security-Policy`, and `X-Frame-Options` leave the app exposed to MIME sniffing, clickjacking, and protocol-downgrade attacks.

