## Summary

`app.js` is a minimal Express server (~20 lines) exposing two GET endpoints (`/health`, `/users`) plus a listener on port 3000. The code itself contains no obvious injection sinks (no DB queries, no `eval`, no shell calls, no template rendering with user input), but several issues are present by *omission* — missing middleware and protections that any production Express app should have. Below is the OWASP-Top-10–aligned breakdown.

