## Summary

`app.js` is a very small Express application with only two endpoints (`/health` and `/users`) plus a server bootstrap. There is **no authentication, no database, no user input handling, no file I/O, and no template rendering**, so the attack surface is minimal. That said, even a small Express app has several real and latent issues worth addressing before this is built out further.

I'll go through actual findings, then preventative recommendations for the OWASP Top 10 categories that will become relevant as this file grows.

